      "independent_solution": "In the conventional uninterrupted constant-individual-speed model on a route of length L>0, let whole-route times be T1,T2>2 hours. The meeting after2 hours gives2L/T1+2L/T2=L, hence1/T1+1/T2=1/2. Since departures are simultaneous and the first arrives later, T1-T2=5/3 hours. Set T2=z and T1=z+5/3:1/z+1/(z+5/3)=1/2 yields3z^2-7z-10=(3z-10)(z+1)=0. Thus z=10/3 or-1. The negative duration is inadmissible; T2=10/3 hours and T1=5 hours.",
